   "text": "The drawing shows magnesium bis(esomeprazole), i.e. two identical 5-methoxybenzimidazolide\u2013sulfinyl\u2013pyridine units with one Mg\u00b2\u207a.\n\n**Each ligand:**\n- **Pyridine ring:** the CH2 on the carbon next to N, then methyl, methoxy and methyl on the next three ring carbons, and a CH next to the methyl at the far end of the ring.\n- **Linker:** the CH2 connects to a sulfoxide S(=O), which is bonded to C2 of the benzimidazole.\n- **Benzimidazole:** one ring nitrogen carries the negative charge ([n-]). The benzo ring has an OCH3 group.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** the only stereocentre is the sulfur. The wedge to the CH2 puts that group toward the viewer. The CIP priorities are O > C2 of the benzimidazole > CH2 > lone pair. Viewed from the front, O \u2192 C2 \u2192 CH2 runs counterclockwise, so the sulfur is S, as in esomeprazole. In SMILES, written as `c(...)[S@@](=O)Cc`, this corresponds to `@@`.\n\nSMILES: [Mg+2].COc1ccc2[n-]c(nc2c1)[S@@](=O)Cc1ncc(C)c(OC)c1C.COc1ccc2[n-]c(nc2c1)[S@@](=O)Cc1ncc(C)c(OC)c1C"
